  "final_text": "I generated `eta_input.dat` for the \u03b7 channel with the requested kinematics. One correction was needed: \u03c6* = 370\u00b0 is outside the conventional [0\u00b0, 360\u00b0) range, so I normalized it to 10\u00b0 (370 \u2212 360). This has no physical effect \u2014 in `exclurad.F`, \u03c6* only ever appears inside `cos()`/`sin()` calls, which are 360\u00b0-periodic, so 370\u00b0 and 10\u00b0 give identical results.\n\nThe rest of the kinematics check out: W = 1.7 GeV is safely above the \u03b7-production threshold (W_thr \u2248 m_p + m_\u03b7 \u2248 1.486 GeV) and within the supported grid, Q\u00b2 = 1.0 GeV\u00b2 and cos \u03b8* = 0.5 are both well within range. The input uses the standard \u03b7-configuration defaults (model 3 = EtaMAID, ivec = 1 recoil proton, bmom = 6.53 GeV, vcut = 0.166 GeV\u00b2). Details are in `outcome.json`."
